    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_4",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "\"How?\" is a song from John Lennon's second solo album \"Imagine\", released in 1971. It is a contemplative song inspired by the Primal Therapy he was undergoing with his wife Yoko Ono, during which he faced many personal questions such as \"How can I go forward when I don't know which way I'm facing?\" This song also shows his thoughts about the world in general (such as \"And the World is so tough; Sometimes I feel I've had enough\").",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.9999999942239491,
      "temperature": 0.9999999942239491,
      "expanded": false,
      "visit_count": 0,
      "persistent": true,
